# The vendored skill tree is copied verbatim from upstream, which mixes CRLF and LF.
# Without an explicit attribute, a Windows commit normalizes those files to LF while a Linux
# sync run rewrites them as CRLF, so the drift check in sync-skills.yml reports changes on
# every run. `text=auto` makes git normalize on both add and diff, so the comparison is
# platform-independent; `eol=lf` keeps shell scripts usable when staged on a Linux runner.
.github/cloud-skills/** text=auto eol=lf
